A small number of short sallies won't necessarily produce a large deviation from range residence. Other behaviors can also violate residence, such as range shifts. I would plot BS620_2015 with the locations colored by time to inspect further.

In the last two examples, I would try zooming the variogram out and seeing if there is a big upwards trend in the variogram at the end, which can also indicate a big range shift.

Best,
Chris

