Hi Nanette,
The webinar was recorded and linked to in the Skype group, which you should be a member of. But that link does expire after 30 days. The Spring webinar will be next month, however.
What are you classifying as an outlier?
The statistics are re-calculated. In either case, the speeds linking each location are similar to distance/time estimates but with an adjustment for the location error: https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2020.06.12.130195v1
Basically, yes. It's using a robust estimate of the average location (geometric median) that doesn't account for autocorrelation, specifically for filtering outliers, but not for further analysis.
Best,
Chris

